<!doctype html><html lang="zh-CN"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Small-template training record path</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#101a29;color:#e7edf7;font:16px/1.8 "Microsoft YaHei",sans-serif}main{max-width:1150px;margin:auto;padding:24px}a{color:#9fd5ff}nav{position:sticky;top:0;background:#172638;padding:12px;z-index:2;display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap}pre{overflow:auto;background:#09131f;padding:16px}code{font:13px/1.7 Consolas,monospace}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto}td,th{border:1px solid #45617e;padding:8px 12px}blockquote{border-left:4px solid #e7b667;margin:18px 0;padding:1px 16px;background:#203249}h1,h2,h3,h4{scroll-margin-top:85px}img{max-width:100%}.meta{font-size:12px;color:#a9bfd3;overflow-wrap:anywhere}summary{cursor:pointer}</style><nav><a href="../../../framework-architecture.html">主架构</a><a href="../../main-ui-map.html">逆向核心</a><a href="../index.html">关联文档目录</a><a data-source-download download href="../../../plugins/GRAY-MATCH-SMALL-TEMPLATE-RECORD-SOURCE.md">下载原始文件</a></nav><main><h1 id="small-template-training-record-path">Small-template training record path</h1><h2 id="explicit-instruction-update">Explicit instruction update</h2><p>Full small-template decoded span is now <code>180bf2610-explicit-span.asm.txt</code>. With prolog delta0x248, original arguments5..20 are atcurrentRSP+0x270 through+0x2e8 in8-byte steps. It confirms argument6 float radians,7 packed destination size,8/9 cropped image/mask pointer outputs,10 stride output,11 crop dimensions,12 float center shift,13 contiguous selected bytes,14/15 double sum/squared-sum outputs,16 pixel count,17 span records,18 span count,19/20 scratch planes. In particular bf2f98/bf2f9f and bf30aa/bf30b1 use CVTSI2SD on signed int32 span totals before double accumulation. Whole-frame double sum of byte products would skip the original per-span conversion boundary.</p>
<p>Raw constants are preserved in <code>small-template-constants.json</code>: lower coordinate boundbitsBC23D70A=-0.01f, upper coordinate bounddimension-minus-bits3F7D70A4(0.99f), cubic constants0.5/5/4/3, pixel max255. Original scan bounds must not be rewritten as generic0..dimension-1.</p>
<p>The parent trainer&#39;s decompiler void signature was caused by Ghidra stopping after security-cookie calls. Newly decoded exact epilogs <code>180bf17e5-explicit-span.asm.txt</code> and <code>180bf1bb2-explicit-span.asm.txt</code> show success XOR EAX,EAX atbf17ee thenRET, and failure MOV EAX,10100000 atbf1bbb thenRET. Parent raw requested0 maps planning depth8 <strong>and retains an auto flag</strong>. Some missing/insufficient layers break with partial actual depth and success for auto, while a manual requested depth returns10100000. The production normalized pyramid cannot replace this higher-level auto/manual quality decision. Success publishes actual layer count/model pointer/used bytes; early failure path does not run those success stores. Additional mask-empty and geometry-specific downstream records remain source questions, not successful runtime evidence.</p>
<p>Original core SHA85D17ECC87D52E9A62D8BB86C8D5208AC999BCD31EC6D0806453F8165733F549; <code>analysis/gray-match/core-boundary/output/180bf2610-bounded.c</code> recovered by isolated read-only Ghidra. First runtime-entry assembly463bytes is only a fragment: full20-argument ABI/output stores still need explicit-span assembly before a callable probe or exact implementation. The source below is a concrete data-flow inventory, not proof of a fully verified signature.</p>
<p>Parent <code>befdc0</code> chooses this path when either working dimension&lt;64. Inputs are image/stride, mask/stride, packed source size, angle in radians, packed destination size, then output pointers/scratch storage. It clears the two destination scratch planes, computes cosf/sinf, forms centered inverse coordinates, and scans destination rows by adding cosf/subtracting sinf per x and adding sinf/cosf per y. Source mask selection uses <code>(int)(coordinate+0.5f)</code>, whereas image interpolation uses truncation plus a clamped four-by-four neighborhood. A generic bilinear/nearest image warp would not reconstruct this path.</p>
<p>For selected pixels it evaluates the original separable four-sample cubic polynomials in float, adds0.5f, clamps to0..255 and converts to int32 then byte. Polynomial operation grouping is explicit in C; the fourth row is grouped differently from the preceding row expressions, so a generic reassociated polynomial helper is not yet justified. Needed raw PE constants are0x16c6814/6830/6834/6838/683c/6840/6844; only those read from the original should be used. x/y bounds, rounding order and zero-selected outputs must be verified from assembly, not mathematical cubic interpolation intent.</p>
<p>It writes both a destination scratch pixel and a contiguous selected-pixel buffer. Consecutive nonzero mask spans become0x18-byte records: row, start x, end x, selected-buffer offset, byte sum, squared-byte sum. The latter two accumulate int32 first, then are converted and accumulated into double when a span closes. Coordinates are subsequently rebased to the bounding crop. Output stores include cropped scratch pointers, destination stride, crop dimensions, center shift, sums, selected-pixel count and span count. Parent records these relative to the model base, including a0x40-byte per-angle header and selected records; this is the missing bridge between training bytes and search statistics.</p>
<p>The no-span path reads source-record state before a nonzero-span guard near the tail in decompiled C. Whether current caller guarantees a selected span after rotation is not established; do not fabricate a zero record or execute unknown empty-span ABI. This is separate from the earlier required-mask contrast predicate. The large-template&gt;=64 path is inlined in <code>befdc0</code> with16.16 coordinate arithmetic; it must not be declared equivalent to this float/cubic path.</p>
<p>Current implementation remains ModelSlots, dot/normalization, limits and normalized1390 pyramid. Angle grouping has a fixed four-table original oracle and a pending production candidate; actual cubic sample/model sparse records and large-template records are not yet implemented. No full trained-model or search equivalence is claimed.</p>
